%I A399173 #68 Nov 06 2026 19:38:19
%S A399173 1,3,6,15,39,98,248,630,1600,4070,10368,26442,67515,172575,441560,
%T A399173 1130857,2898702,7436201,19090910,49046529,126088677,324348438,
%U A399173 834831336,2149916450,5539445639,14279731083,36827387506,95018472827,245256977205,633288486288
%N A399173 First column of the derivative-compositional Riordan array psi_1(f) = (f^[1](x)*(f^[1])'(x)/x, f^[1](x)) = (f(x)*f'(x)/x, f(x)), where f(x) = x*s(x) and s(x) is the g.f. of A004148 (RNA secondary structures).
%C A399173 a(n) is the number of ordered pairs (W_0, W_1) of peakless lattice walks (steps N=(0,1), S=(0,-1), E=(1,0), starting and ending on the x-axis, never going below it, and with no N step immediately followed by an S step), of total length n, together with a distinguished gap in W_0 (a walk of length j has j+1 gaps).
%C A399173 For k >= 1, the derivative-compositional array is psi_k(f) = (f^[k](x)*(f^[k])'(x)/x, f^[k](x)), where f^[k] denotes the k-fold compositional iterate f o f o ... o f (not the k-th derivative). This sequence is column 0 of psi_1(f) for f(x) = x*s(x), the derivative-compositional image of the RNA I Riordan array (s(x), x*s(x)); the case k = 2 is A400355.
%D A399173 I. Madu and A. Nkwanta, Powers of the RNA Riordan Array: Derivative-Compositional Images and Colored Peakless Walks, unpublished manuscript, 2026.
%D A399173 A. Nkwanta, Lattice paths and RNA secondary structures, DIMACS Series in Discrete Mathematics and Theoretical Computer Science, Vol. 34 (1997), 137-147.
%D A399173 L. W. Shapiro, S. Getu, W.-J. Woan, and L. C. Woodson, The Riordan group, Discrete Applied Mathematics, Vol. 34 (1991), 229-239.
%H A399173 Ifeyinwa Madu, <a href="/A399173/b399173.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..50</a>
%F A399173 G.f.: A(x) = f(x)*f'(x)/x = (1/(2*x)) * d/dx (x*s(x))^2, where s(x) = (1 - x + x^2 - sqrt(1 - 2*x - x^2 - 2*x^3 + x^4))/(2*x^2) is the g.f. of A004148.
%F A399173 a(n) = ((n+2)/2) * [x^n] s(x)^2.
%F A399173 a(n) = Sum_{j=0..n} (j+1)*A004148(j)*A004148(n-j).
%F A399173 a(n) = (n+2) * Sum_{p=0..floor((n-1)/2)} binomial(n-p-1,p)*binomial(n-p+1,n-2*p-1)/(n-2*p) for n >= 1.
%F A399173 a(n) ~ c * ((3+sqrt(5))/2)^n / sqrt(n), where c = (9+4*sqrt(5))*sqrt((7*sqrt(5)-15)/2)/(2*sqrt(Pi)) = 2.891266...
%F A399173 a(n) = binomial(n+2,2) + (terms with p >= 1 in the sum above); the difference a(n) - binomial(n+2,2) begins 0, 0, 0, 5, 24, 77, 220, 594.
%e A399173 a(3) = 1*A004148(0)*A004148(3) + 2*A004148(1)*A004148(2) + 3*A004148(2)*A004148(1) + 4*A004148(3)*A004148(0) = 2 + 2 + 3 + 8 = 15.
%o A399173 (PARI) a(n) = if(n==0, 1, (n+2)*sum(p=0, (n-1)\2, binomial(n-p-1,p)*binomial(n-p+1,n-2*p-1)/(n-2*p)));
%Y A399173 Cf. A004148, A400355.
%K A399173 nonn,easy,new
%O A399173 0,2
%A A399173 _Ifeyinwa Madu_, Oct 30 2026
